sabrina carpenter is the queen of glow  ups  she's so talented that the most  challenging part of filming her new  movie work it was trying to be  bad at dancing but the road to stardom  isn't an easy one  especially when you end up with big  disney channel expectations  thankfully sabrina's used to the drama  and has tons of talented friends  supporting her  from being a little red-headed guest  star in austin and ally to how she's  trying to inspire women to have it all  today  here's how sabrina has grown up in the  spotlight and what big plans are next on  her to-do list  let's pretend that i'm actually 15 so  this doesn't feel as embarrassing  it seems like only yesterday we were  watching little lucy gluckman stun  on austin and ally and now sabrina has  grown into a full-blown disney channel  icon  she started performing when she was only  11 but now sabrina carpenter is 21 years  old and ready to put her disney days  behind her  even though she'll always have love for  her disney channel roots  and we'll always be up for a girl meets  world marathon  but being a disney star comes with a lot  of expectations and sabrina is still  trying as an adult to finally shake them  off  so let's have a look at what her  career's been like so far  sabrina grew up in pennsylvania dancing  five or six times a week  she was always a performer and an  incredibly hard worker  landing her first disney channel role in  2011 on  austin and alley as lucy gluckman in the  episode  moon weeks and mentors just a year later  she landed a voice credit on phineas and  ferb  and then by 2014 it was official sabrina  would star as maya hart in a major  disney channel spin-off  girl meets world remember how we all  freaked out because boy meets world was  finally getting a female-centric redo  well sabrina was busy being both excited  and terrified by her first real shot in  the spotlight  it was actually hannah montana that  inspired sabrina to chase her dreams  and give her the confidence to become a  multi-talented performer  in an interview with in the nose gibson  johns she talked about how she was only  six years old and watching the pilot  episode  and that's when her dreams really  started to become clear like hannah  and most of us obsessed with the show  sabrina wanted to sing  dance and act she also daydreamed about  wearing all of hannah and miley's crazy  colorful costumes  which is something we definitely have in  common sabrina went on to say that she  gets jealous when she watches people act  in movies or perform  because she wants to be the one on the  stage she really was born for the  spotlight  but even though she knew she was great  sabrina had no idea what was coming her  way  she even got to star in her own disney  channel original movie  adventures in babysitting joining the  ranks of other dcom stars like demi  lovato and selena gomez but as she got  older sabrina decided it was finally  time to put the disney days behind her  though she did tell teen vogue that she  enjoyed coming into herself while  playing a character that was also  growing up  plus we got to see her grow up alongside  us imagine how different our childhoods  would have been without sabrina on our  tvs  nowadays sabrina refers to disney as the  d word  she doesn't enjoy re-watching her old  shows especially girl meets world but  only because she doesn't always feel  like it reflects who she is as a person  now  plus it's strange to see your younger  more awkward self dressed in crazy  outfits and doing eccentric things on  screen  would you really want to watch your  middle school self try to tackle fame  and do televised interviews  yeah didn't think so now sabrina's moved  on to another major television and film  company that's giving her more freedom  to be who she wants to be  you might have heard of this little old  streaming service called netflix  first she appeared as harper crayman in  tallgirl but with workit  she finally has her starring role in a  netflix movie  in the film which sabrina describes as a  new generation's version of step  up sabrina plays quinn an overachiever  with a 4.0 gpa  and some huge college aspirations when  duke university says her  extracurriculars suck  she ends up forming her own dance troupe  alongside liza koshy and jordan  fisher it's a huge opportunity for  sabrina who gets to cement herself as a  netflix star  and work alongside some of the most  famous young faces today  plus we get to see another dancing movie  and there are never  too many right dancing was the biggest  challenge for sabrina while filming but  not  in the way you might think it was  challenging for her to have to be bad at  dancing  she told cosmo that dancing badly might  be harder than dancing well  we don't know about you but being bad at  dancing would have come completely  naturally to us thankfully sabrina was  up for the challenge and cites channing  tatum as one of her celeb crushes  that helped inspire her to be in a  dancing movie channing tatum is also one  of  our celeb crushes but we probably won't  be getting any invitations from netflix  to star in a dance movie  oh well now that she's made her journey  from disney to netflix  sabrina is eyeing the next big thing she  has four pop albums out  and even a few dramas like the short  history of the long road  and the hate you give on her resume plus  she was a producer on work it  making her a star who can sing act dance  and  work behind the scenes a true quadruple  threat  but are you even surprised however being  21 and growing up famous  isn't easy so sabrina has also had to  weather a few storms to get as far as  she has  she spoke with elle recently about  embracing being an adult and her fears  she explained that she used to be  fearless  at auditions when she was young and now  auditioning and getting rejected is  becoming harder and harder but she's  opening up about these feelings so that  young women everywhere know that  self-doubt is completely normal in the  past few years she's learned that being  a disney channel star  isn't all sunshine and rainbows she not  only had to deal with huge fame at a  young age but she also lost her good  friend  cameron boyce in 2019 while 2020 marked  the passing of her grandfather  now she's struggling with being not busy  enough while studios figure out what's  next  in an uncertain world but doing promo  for work it in quarantine has been her  saving grace  especially when it involves her awesome  friends like liza koshy  sabrina also turns to jordan fisher and  joey king for support  that's definitely a group of friends  we'd love to hang out with  she told teen vogue that supporting your  friends is a gift  we couldn't agree more sabrina while  sabrina would rather focus on  friendships the media has always hounded  her about relationships  just imagine how embarrassing and  dramatic trying to date was in high  school  and multiply that times a thousand it  all started when sabrina was linked to  her girl meets world co-star  corey foglemanis though she put those  rumors to rest by saying their love was  completely platonic  she's also been linked to her tall girl  co-star griffin gluck  and riverdale star casey cott who  starred in her why music video  but since her split from good luck  charlie star bradley stephen perry in  2015  she's mostly been single and living her  very best life  so what's next for the rising star well  work it may be all fun and games sabrina  wants to take on the serious stuff too  the stuff that comments on the way that  society works and that really inspires  change  like the short history of the long road  and the hate you give  reflecting on haley her hate you give  character now  sabrina told teen vogue that she's proud  to play a character that can be a mirror  for some people  as harsh as that may seem sabrina's not  afraid to take on the tough roles and we  all know that sometimes  you gotta see the bad to really  recognize the good that's out there  and to make serious changes that'll make  the world a better place  as a first-time producer on workit  sabrina is now thinking about how she  wants to keep  exploring the behind-the-scenes creative  process of creating movies and  television  right before we all got stuck in  quarantine she was starring in mean  girls on broadway as katie herron she  only got to perform two nights but she  hopes that as soon as things go back to  normal she can continue her broadway  dreams  and if they cast a musical mean girls  movie she'd be our first choice to star  so from a small red-headed aspiring  performer to a confident blonde  bombshell  sabrina carpenter has definitely done a  good job of growing up  in the spotlight she's gorgeous healthy  and happy  on the inside and the outside but she  knows that being a star is always work  and she's willing to put in the hours  with her amazing friends and fans  cheering her on  what do you think the next decade of her  life will look like how does it feel  watching sabrina carpenter blow up  right before our eyes let us know your  favorite rules from the work it stars  career in the comments  don't forget to hit that like button and  subscribe to the things for more  thanks for watching and we'll see you  next time
 

